                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Rock Solid Shoot'em up here. Maybe a bit on the easy side for the hard core folks, but with that comes a lot more easing for people not so hardcore like myself to appreciate. Or at least, I found the skill to at least play though on Winnie Hut Jr. But I plan on doing a few more runs with a little more friction just because I love the sound design, presentation, and creative bullet patterns. Which is what I tend to look for in a indie shmup. So I'd say if you are looking for more of a quick arcade shoot'em up romp, you can get that here. And if you are looking for a solid ICC, you can probably also get that here. And, that is pretty important given we ain't got that Arcade stuff much anymore.\n\nThe sound is a delight. I know its more so from Amiga and such but for me I read Sega Genesis which I'm a big fan of in terms of the sound chip (when it isn't a screeching nightmare box). The sprite work and color are all gorgeous and I seldom found myself unable to read the bullets because of the splash of Cave in there.\n\nAnd as suggested, the quality is there in terms of level and means of practicing and accessibility. I felt pretty good with my Weenie Hut General run, which I normally get when I do something like Radian Silvergun on easy. Its still pretty hard. Idk what I'm saying. I liked this one a lot, so I'm throwing a review to boost the numbers. But by no means in bad faith. You can get pro-oppinons on it and yeah, they also seem to like it. So, good times.",
